Sval: let several overflowable toolbars share one overflow button, hide what overflows, and order their own items

The toolbar in the Workspace panel is a set of pills, each a toolbar of
its own that gives items up as the panel narrows. They share one overflow
button and panel, so only the first toolbar wires the button; a pill whose
items are reached another way hides them in a list never shown
(`overflowhides`); each pill names the items that may leave it, in order
(`overfloworder`), since the same widget leaves the header row by other
rules, and names different items for different layouts, so an item its
order no longer lets leave comes back first; and in the panel's narrowest
layout each pill gives up all it may (`overflowall`). A pill takes an item
back once the item fits beside what the pill shows, which holds whichever
layout sent it out. A pill checks again as its order or `overflowall`
changes, and as it narrows with the panel, neither of which resizes the
window.

